GUNK RADAR: DATA BEHIND RUBY, THE AI GUIDE
==========================================
Every source Ruby uses to answer visitors, and the results of cross-checking that data against
the original publishers.

Last checked: 2026-10-18
Map data (terrain, rivers, crops, etc.) is documented separately in DATA_SOURCES.md.


1. HOW RUBY GETS HER ANSWERS
----------------------------
Ruby answers in two ways:

  a) Scripted lines (no AI). When you pick a city, a factory, or an "affected area" button, her
     words are built directly from each factory's facility.json and impacts.json.

  b) Typed questions (AI). These go to Google Gemini (model: gemini-3.5-flash-lite by default,
     set by GEMINI_MODEL) through web/src/app/api/chat/route.ts. Before every answer, the server
     gives Gemini the study notes listed in section 2 (about 48,000 characters). Gemini is
     told to answer only from those notes and to say "I don't know" otherwise. As a language
     model it can still draw on general knowledge, so typed answers are not guaranteed to come
     only from the notes.


2. FILES RUBY READS
-------------------
All under cities/. The chat server loads them once and sends them with every typed question.

  cities/README.md                         Overview: cross-cutting findings, summary table, sources
  cities/green_bay/README.md               Local setting: rivers, cleanups, beaches, drinking water
  cities/manitowoc/README.md               Local setting for Manitowoc
  cities/sheboygan/README.md               Local setting for Sheboygan
  cities/milwaukee/README.md               Local setting for Milwaukee

  For each of the 12 factories, in cities/<city>/<company>/:
    facility.json    Name, address, location, 2024 on-site releases (total / air / water / land),
                     top chemicals
    impacts.json     Plain-language "affected areas": what is affected, how, and how to avoid it
                     (each tip has its text, plus a picture and short title for the
                     "How to protect yourself" box beside Ruby; the pictures and titles
                     are hand-picked, not data. Most tips also link to the official page
                     or DNR phone line for acting on them. The "Report …" tips open the
                     community forum on that factory, where the company can reply)
    research.md      Full write-up: chemicals, where they go, people and schools nearby,
                     compliance record

  The 12 factories:
    Green Bay   Georgia-Pacific Broadway (georgia_pacific_broadway)        TRI ID 54307FRTHW1919S
                CNG Green Bay (cng_green_bay)
                Green Bay Packaging Coated Products (green_bay_packaging)
    Manitowoc   Manitowoc Public Utilities (manitowoc_public_utilities)
                Jagemann Plating (jagemann_plating)
                Eck Industries (eck_industries)
    Sheboygan   Edgewater Generating Station (edgewater_generating_station)
                Hexion Sheboygan (hexion_sheboygan)
                SACO AEI (saco_aei)
    Milwaukee   Seidel Tanning (seidel_tanning)
                Highline Warren (highline_warren)
                Advanced Plating Technologies (advanced_plating_technologies)

  Ruby does not read these supporting files directly. They are the raw evidence the notes
  were written from:
    echo_facility_report.json         EPA ECHO report (permits, compliance, demographics)
    echo_effluent_<permit>.json       EPA ECHO water-discharge data (Georgia-Pacific, Edgewater)
    schools_nearby.json               Schools within 1 and 3 miles
    model.json                        3D building shape (map only, no facts)


3. ORIGINAL DATA SOURCES
------------------------
  EPA Toxics Release Inventory (TRI), Basic Data File, Wisconsin, reporting year 2024
    https://www.epa.gov/toxics-release-inventory-tri-program/tri-basic-data-files-calendar-years-1987-present
    Download: https://data.epa.gov/efservice/downloads/tri/mv_tri_basic_download/2024_WI/csv
    Used for: which 12 factories (top 3 per city by on-site releases), every pound figure, chemicals,
    air / water / land split, transfers to sewer plants and off-site
    Local copy: background/raw/tri_2024_wi.csv (trimmed to the columns used)

  EPA ECHO Detailed Facility Reports (one per factory)
    https://echo.epa.gov/
    API: https://echodata.epa.gov/echo/dfr_rest_services.get_dfr?output=JSON&p_id=<FRS registry ID>
    Used for: residents within 1 mile and their make-up (ECHO's ACS 2024 demographics),
    permits, inspections, quarters out of compliance, notices, enforcement cases, impaired
    waters, ozone non-attainment status, reported water-discharge loads
    Pulled 2026-10-17; compliance data through 09/2026

  EPA ECHO effluent charts (water-permit measurements)
    API: https://echodata.epa.gov/echo/eff_rest_services.get_effluent_chart?p_id=<permit>
    Used for: real limit exceedances vs. late or missing reports (permits WI0001848, WI0001589)
    Period 07/2023 to 10/2026

  NCES EDGE public and private school locations, 2023-24 school year
    https://nces.ed.gov/programs/edge/Geographic/SchoolLocations
    Used for: schools within 1 and 3 miles of each factory

  USGS National Hydrography Dataset (river and stream lines)
    https://hydro.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/nhd/MapServer
    Used for: distance from each Milwaukee factory to the nearest river

  Google Gemini (typed answers only; see section 1b)
    https://ai.google.dev/


